// Title: Permission Check Via Accesschk.EXE
// ID: c625d754-6a3d-4f65-9c9a-536aea960d37
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: Teymur Kheirkhabarov (idea), Mangatas Tondang, oscd.community, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2020-10-13
// Tags: attack.discovery, attack.t1069.001
// Description: Detects the usage of the "Accesschk" utility, an access and privilege audit tool developed by SysInternal and often being abused by attacker to verify process privileges
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "uwcqv ") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "kwsu ") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "qwsu ") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "uwdqs "))) AND ((where(Product IENDSWITH "AccessChk")) OR (where(Description ICONTAINS "Reports effective permissions")) OR ((where(Image IENDSWITH "\\accesschk.exe") OR where(Image IENDSWITH "\\accesschk64.exe") OR where(Image IENDSWITH "\\accesschk64a.exe"))) OR (where(OriginalFileName = "accesschk.exe"))))
